+E-LITE shaders 5.1.3 - CouncilCraft edit
+=========================================
+
+This is a MODIFIED copy of E-LITE shaders 5.1.3 (MakeUp edit). It is not an
+official E-LITE or MakeUp release; please report problems with it to
+CouncilCraft (https://github.com/JaydensAssistant/councilcraft), not to the
+original authors.
+
+Original work:
+- MakeUp - Ultra Fast by Javier Garduño
+  https://github.com/javiergcim/MakeUpUltraFast
+- E-LITE shaders (MakeUp edit) by Entokito
+  https://modrinth.com/shader/lite-shaders
+License: GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 or later, unchanged (see
+LICENSE). All original files, notices and credits (Credits, "Credits by
+Entokito", README.md) are kept as they were.
+
+Modified by: CouncilCraft, 2026-10-25 (shipped in CouncilCraft 0.4.15 as the
+"Medium" graphics preset).
+
+Why: in Immersive Portals portal views the stock TAA history belongs to
+another view (IP renders portal views through the same Iris pipeline), which
+left pale blue/white halos around foliage edges. This edit rewrites the TAA
+history rejection; everything else is stock E-LITE 5.1.3.
+
+Modified files (all changes marked "CouncilCraft patch"):
+- shaders/lib/fast_taa.glsl
+    fast_taa() and fast_taa_depth() (Denoise, TAA and Sharp TAA, with and
+    without DOF) share cc_taa_resolve():
+    * history clipped to a tight 3x3 min/max box intersected with a variance
+      box in YCoCg (stock: loose sphere around 4 neighbours);
+    * 3x3 depth-discontinuity check on VANILLA depth only (depthtex1,
+      linearised with gbufferProjectionInverse); sky and DH terrain count as
+      "very far", the same way stock composite2 sees them -> much less
+      history on depth edges, less again while the camera moves;
+    * LESS history at high-contrast colour edges (stock used more);
+    * history weight scaled down when it had to be clipped far, and dropped
+      for off-screen reprojection, NaN/huge values, or a camera jump > 8
+      blocks per frame.
+    * with Distant Horizons, pixels whose whole 3x3 is at or
+      beyond the vanilla->DH fade band (or sky) blend smoothly back to the
+      STOCK resolve (60%..85% of the fade start). The fade band is a temporal
+      dither (vanilla fragments discarded by shifted_dither13) that needs the
+      stock TAA to average it out.
+- shaders/common/composite2_fragment.glsl
+    * declares far + dhNearPlane when DISTANT_HORIZONS (fade-band start).
+    * DH terrain is reprojected exactly like stock.
+
+No options, option lists, defaults, buffers or formats were changed, so
+existing settings files (e.g. AA_TYPE=3) still import. History depth is not
+stored in colortex3 alpha (R11F_G11F_B10F with HDR; alpha used by DOF).
+
+The AABB history clip (cc_clip_aabb) is the well-known clip from Playdead's
+INSIDE temporal reprojection (https://github.com/playdeadgames/temporal, MIT).
+No code from other shader packs is included.
+
+The complete change is the patch docs/patches/elite-5.1.3-councilcraft-taa.diff
+in the CouncilCraft repository; applying it to the stock E-LITE 5.1.3 zip from
+Modrinth gives this pack.
