+CouncilCraft patch v2a (2026-10-25, LGPL-3.0): history rejection rewrite.
+Immersive Portals renders portal views through the same Iris pipeline, so the
+TAA history (colortex3) and previous-frame matrices can belong to a different
+view. The stock resolve (loose sphere clamp around 4 neighbours, more history
+at high-contrast edges, no depth test) let that stale history leak in as pale
+halos around foliage. This version, modelled on Complementary's taa.glsl:
+  - clips history to a tight 3x3 min/max box intersected with a variance box
+    (YCoCg, same colour space as stock),
+  - detects depth discontinuities in the current 3x3 (vanilla depth only,
+    sky / Distant Horizons count as "very far", exactly like stock sees them)
+    and uses much less history there,
+  - uses LESS history at high-contrast edges (stock used more),
+  - drops history that had to be clipped far, that reprojects off screen,
+    is NaN/Inf, or when the camera "teleported" between frames.
+v2a: with Distant Horizons, pixels whose whole 3x3 lies in or beyond the
+vanilla->DH dithered fade band (or sky) use the STOCK resolve again. That band
+is a per-frame dither (solid_blocks_fragment.glsl discards vanilla fragments
+with shifted_dither13) that only looks smooth because TAA averages it; the v1
+depth/clip rejection refused to average it and showed the raw dither.
+v2a also linearises vanilla depth with gbufferProjectionInverse (v1 used the
+`far` uniform, which is the render distance, not the real 4x far plane).
+Requires (declared in composite2_fragment.glsl): colortex1, colortex3,
+depthtex1, gbufferProjectionInverse, cameraPosition, previousCameraPosition,
+viewWidth, viewHeight, pixelSizeX, pixelSizeY, and far + dhNearPlane when
+DISTANT_HORIZONS.
 */
 
